      "text": " Validation checks, performance metrics, and result summaries. Results summary should be a table or list of key metrics (ementia, performance, and result summary). Results summary should be a table or list of key metrics (e.g., baseline, performance gain, result summary). Results summary should be a table or instructions to write a short paragraph describing the result (e.g., \"The new benchmark X achieved a 15% improvement over the baseline...\").\n\nWrite a short technical guide... (the rest of the prompt). So we need to produce a short technical guide covering all those points.\n\nWe must ensure we include:\n\n- Where to put scripts, data, notes, patches, result summaries.\n- How to name run directories.\n- What to record for reproducibility.\n- How to decide whether a result is valid enough to promote.\n- Validation checks.\n- Performance metrics.\n- Result summaries (table or list of key metrics).\n- Instructions to write a short paragraph describing the result.\n\nThus the guide should be organized with headings: Overview, Directory Structure, Adding a Benchmark, Naming Conventions, Reproducibility, Validation & Metrics, Promotion Criteria, Example Workflow.\n\nMake sure to mention specifics: e.g., scripts go under `benchmarks/scripts/`, data under `benchmarks/{name}/data/`, notes under `benchmarks/{name}/notes/`, patches under `benchmarks/{name}/patches/`, result summaries under `benchmarks/{name}/results/`. Run directories: e.g., `benchmarks/mybench/run/` with subfolders for each run (e.g., `baseline/`, `new_optimizer/`). Or use a top-level run folder with subfolders for each configuration.\n\nAlso mention that each benchmark should have a `README.md` describing the benchmark, its purpose, how to run, expected outputs.\n\nValidation checks: ensure deterministic execution, same hardware, same random seeds, same environment (e.g., Docker container). Use `make run` or `python run.py`. Check that the output files are present and have correct format.\n\nPerformance metrics: baseline time, new time, speedup, memory usage, etc. Record in a table.\n\nResult summary: a table with columns: Benchmark, Baseline Time, New Time, Speedup, Memory, Notes. Or a list of key metrics.\n\nPromotion criteria: speedup > X% (maybe 10%?), reproducibility",
      "text_preview": " Validation checks, performance metrics, and result summaries. Results summary should be a table or list of key metrics (ementia, performance, and result summary). Results summary should be a table or list of key metrics (e.g., baseline, performance gain, result summary). Results summary should be a table or instructio",
